        <item>
            <title>2.11.0</title>
            <pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 22:51:35 +0900</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/Saqoosha/Canopy</link>
            <sparkle:version>80</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.11.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[### Features

- **Session recap.** When you come back to Canopy after being away for a few minutes, a one-line "where we left off" note now appears directly above the chat input for each visible session. It summarizes what the session was doing so you can pick up without re-reading the transcript, and it clears the moment you send your next message.
  - This mirrors the Claude Code CLI's away-summary behavior, which never reached Canopy on its own.
  - The recap does not consume your session's context window, and it never appears as a message in the transcript — including after you close and reopen the session.
- **Settings toggle.** Session recaps can be turned off under Settings → General.
]]></description>
